# Presence of this file turns on hooks/pre-gh-outbound-leak-gate.sh for this repo.
#
# This repo is shared, outlives any single engagement, and may be public. Nothing
# published from it — PR titles and bodies, issue text, release notes — may carry
# a client or product name, a ticket identifier, an internal repo, service, table
# or flag name, or a path that exists only in someone else's codebase.
#
# It blocks two classes with no configuration: the ticket-key shape (letters, a
# hyphen, digits) and the names of the projects you work in, derived from the list
# the harness already maintains — so a new engagement is covered the day it starts.
# ~/.claude/leak-patterns is optional, for a name no directory spells out.
#
# A lesson that needs the original named is not yet a rule. Generalize it.
#
# `allow: <glob>` exempts a path from the staged-CONTENT scan. Commit messages are
# never exempt. Only the gates' own suites belong here: a matcher cannot be tested
# without fixtures shaped like the thing it matches, and blocking the commit that
# adds them would leave the bypass as the only way forward.
allow: tests/pre-commit-leak-gate.test.sh
allow: tests/pre-gh-outbound-leak-gate.test.sh
